# Printer not printing

## Symptom
The user clicks Print but nothing comes out. The job stays in the queue, or the printer shows as "Offline".

## Possible causes
- A stuck job in the print queue
- The Print Spooler service (the program that manages print jobs) has stopped
- The printer is off, or its cable or Wi-Fi connection is lost
- The wrong printer is selected

## Resolution
1. Check that the printer is on, has paper and ink, and is connected.
2. Open Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners. Select the printer, click "Open print queue", and cancel any stuck jobs.
3. Press Windows key + R, type `services.msc` and press Enter. Find "Print Spooler", right-click it and select "Restart".
4. Print a test page from the printer's properties.

## Verification
The test page prints and the user can print their own document.

## Escalation
If the Print Spooler keeps stopping, or several users have the same problem on the same printer, escalate to the next support level.
